From 3353c5254ff2d3ab7c35a82196538e81271c2b3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:13:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: a seek step left out while the video of the seek
 before it gets in sync is made once it is

The player leaves out an inaccurate seek (a step forward or back, a big
step, a percentage) that comes within 2 s of the seek before it while
the video of that seek is not in sync yet, so that steps asked for faster
than the video can follow do not pile up. A step pressed while the
picture of the step before it was still coming did nothing at all: the
second "-1 minute" of two, a few presses in a row of which only some
were made. The log said so ("left out, the video of the seek before it
is not in sync yet") and nothing else came of it.

Now the last step left out so is kept (CSeekLeftOut) and made once the
video is in sync, as an absolute seek to its target: where the playback
was shown when it was asked for, plus the step. Its message's ticket
goes with it (CSeekPending), so meanwhile the time reported is its
target, and a step asked for after it goes from there, as for a seek on
its way. Two steps of -1 minute end 2 minutes back, ten end 10 minutes
back, -1 minute then +30 s end 30 s back. It is thrown away, and the log
says why, if anything else comes first: another seek, a seek to a
chapter, a pause or another speed, a flush of the streams, another file,
the player stopping, or the video not getting in sync within 5 s of it.
It is made once at most, and nothing changes where no step is left out.
Said in the log when it is kept, made or thrown away.

Reported by skull-01 (a second -1 minute that did not move).
